# JUSTLOVEJAZZ — Cursor rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md) for the full agent operating procedure.
This file is a quick reference; it does not duplicate AGENTS.md.

## Stack

- **Runtime:** Bun + Vite 8 + TypeScript 6 (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`)
- **3D:** Three.js 0.184 with TSL NodeMaterials, WebGPU → WebGL2 fallback
- **UI:** UIkit 3 (component/layout/a11y baseline), Less
- **Test:** Vitest (unit), Playwright (E2E), Lighthouse CI

## Hard constraints

- TSL NodeMaterials only — no raw `ShaderMaterial`.
- `renderer.setAnimationLoop` — no app-owned `requestAnimationFrame` loop.
- Inline splash in `index.html`; Enter disabled until `jlz:webgl-ready`.
- EnvSphere is the background owner; ground plane is contact-section only.
- Six-section model: Lab, Intro, About, Works, Contact, Menu (fixed order).
- WebGPU/WebGL fallback based on the renderer actually created.
- Dispose all listeners, timers, GPU resources in `dispose()`/`destroy()`.
- Reduced-motion: authored animations must snap to settled state synchronously.
- UIkit 3 first — see [docs/UIKIT3.md](../../../docs/UIKIT3.md) solution
  priority order before writing custom CSS.
- Typed events (`jlz:webgl-ready/failed`, `jlz:section-change`,
  `jlz:route-change`) use `eventBus.emit()`. Other `jlz:*` are local DOM
  contracts via `window.dispatchEvent`.

## Verification gate

```bash
bun run type-check && bun run lint && bun run test:unit && bun run build
```

CI runs the same gate plus Playwright E2E + Lighthouse on every push/PR to
`main`.

## Commit style

Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`,
`chore:`, `perf:`. Scope optional: `feat(works):`, `fix(overlay):`.

## Before editing

1. `git status --short` — preserve unrelated work.
2. Read the relevant doc from [docs/README.md](../../../docs/README.md)
   ownership map.
3. Use `rg` for search.
4. After edits, run the verification gate.
